Package: FDC2Qt
Title: Synthetic Streamflow Series Generation through a Regional Regression Tool based on Flow-Duration Curves
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Alan", "Spadoni", email = "alan.spadoni2@unibo.it", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0007-2411-9507"))
    person("Attilio", "Castellarin", email = "attilio.castellarin@unibo.it", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6111-0612"))
Description: Generates hydrologically consistent synthetic daily and hourly
    streamflow series in ungauged or scarcely gauged catchments, using
    morpho-climatic catchment descriptors and hydrometric data from gauged
    catchments (daily and hourly streamflows, mean annual flows, hourly
    stream stages and rating curves). For an ungauged site, a regional
    period-of-record flow duration curve is estimated with an index-flow
    approach (Castellarin et al., 2004), as the product of the mean annual
    flow, predicted by stepwise multiple regression on catchment
    descriptors (Efroymson, 1960), and a dimensionless curve obtained as a
    weighted average of gauged-catchment curves, with weights proportional to
    an hydrological similarity measure(region-of-influence approach;
    Burn, 1990). Daily streamflows are then derived from a donor gauged
    catchment through nonlinear interpolation on flow-duration curves
    (Smakhtin et al., 1997). Hourly streamflows are obtained by linear
    interpolation for low flows and second-order polynomials for the
    rising and falling limbs of high-flow events, constrained by hydrograph
    continuity, mass cobservation, passage through the peak and shape of 
    the hydrograph (Maione et al., 2003).
